# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform. This repository is
# developed on Windows, where core.autocrlf normally rewrites text files to CRLF on
# checkout — and a CRLF `check.sh` fails on its first line under WSL with the singularly
# unhelpful `$'\r': command not found`, because the shebang picks up the carriage return.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The PowerShell counterpart has the opposite requirement in principle, but PowerShell
# accepts either, so this only pins what git already does on Windows.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
